The data recorder wants to dump in response to SIGBUS in any thread,
so it must be unblocked in the main loop.

XXX: this restriction appears to have been something historical
related to the MCE handling to force MCEs out of the main thread,
however, the signal handler appears to be able to matchup to vCPU
threads regardless. Find someone with more knowledge to sanity
check this change, as we really want to catch BUS errors from all
threads, not merely vCPU threads.

Signed-off-by: Daniel P. Berrangé <berrange@redhat.com>
---
 util/main-loop.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/util/main-loop.c b/util/main-loop.c
index 65e5dbcc941..8d531f5ec90 100644
--- a/util/main-loop.c
+++ b/util/main-loop.c
@@ -99,7 +99,6 @@ static int qemu_signal_init(Error **errp)
     sigaddset(&set, SIG_IPI);
     sigaddset(&set, SIGIO);
     sigaddset(&set, SIGALRM);
-    sigaddset(&set, SIGBUS);
     /* SIGINT cannot be handled via signalfd, so that ^C can be used
      * to interrupt QEMU when it is being run under gdb.  SIGHUP and
      * SIGTERM are also handled asynchronously, even though it is not
